      "math_academy_id": "e-8555",
      "problem": "Given that $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 15\\right),$ compute $P(2 \\leq X \\leq 3).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14165669/assets/f6d63dbadaa245c39e6d8ee449730351db7679c38cd594c6f425955bff32b562.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 15\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14165669/assets/de6363d39558bf5974b9424cdcc45de05b685724f87f560c0e7a59051dd74ca5.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in \\{2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{1}(\\frac{1}{5})+{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
